<title>FRANCE: Sidel up in heavy trade.</title>
<headline>Sidel up in heavy trade.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in steelmaker Sidel were up 8.50 francs at 329.50 at 1410 GMT in brisk trading.</p>
<p>Traders attributed the rise to the group's recent presentation to U.S. investors and some mentioned talk that the group had won a big contract with Coca-Cola in Asia. Others said it was due for a rebound after a sharp fall in September on disappointing half-year results.</p>
<p>Officials at the company were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>Turnover totalled 590,300 shares.</p>
